Looking at the feedback: the animation feels mechanical and predictable. I need to make the motion organic — varied timing per spark, non-uniform trajectories with noise/wobble, staggered launches so the digit builds up progressively, subtle holding jitter and flicker, variable eruption intervals, and imperfect shatter-return paths. Plus continuous ambient life (bubbling embers, breathing crater glow, twinkling stars, drifting smoke) so the frame is never static between eruptions.

Key organic changes:
- **Per-spark randomness**: each spark has its own ascent duration (0.7–1.2s), wobble amplitude (1.5–4), phase seeds, birth delay — no two sparks follow the same path
- **Staggered arrival**: sparks launch at different sub-times within the eruption, so digits grow pixel-by-pixel, not all-at-once
- **Curved rising paths**: two-frequency sine wobble on the ascent, decaying as the spark nears its target, with vertical jitter too
- **Randomized targets**: each eruption shuffles the target assignment, so no two cycles look alike
- **Escape sparks**: 5–8 embers per eruption miss the digit entirely and arc off as ballistic fire
- **Holding life**: once formed, digit sparks jitter around their pixel (two-frequency noise) and flicker with cooling
- **Shatter variation**: each spark begins shattering at a slightly different time, with its own random burst direction and duration
- **Variable eruption intervals**: 5.5–8s randomized; also triggers on minute change
- **Ambient continuous activity**: small bubbling embers rise constantly from the crater between eruptions
- **Breathing crater + launch pulse**: crater glow pulses on its own cycle and flares with launches
- **Twinkling stars, drifting smoke**: background always moves

